{title: Come To The Table}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: G}
{tempo: 129}

>Lyrics

Introduction

Verse 1

Come to the table,

There is room for all.

The bread is served,

The wine is poured.

Behold our Savior

Hear His loving call,

He shows The Way,

He is The Door.

Chorus

We are invited now

So let us enter in.

No one denied,

None turned away.

The Savior calls to us

So let the feast begin,

Enter the everlasting day.

Verse 2

Come to the table,

leave your past behind,

Lay all your cares before His throne.

Abundant mercy,

His forgiveness find,

Rejoice in your eternal home!

(Repeat chorus)

We are invited now

So let us enter in.

No one denied,

None turned away.

The Savior calls to us

So let the feast begin,

Enter the everlasting day.

(Raise key)

Verse 3

Come to the table,

Bring your neighbors, too.

Plead with them all to come inside.

Tell of the One

Who makes each heart brand new,

In whom our souls are satisfied!

(Repeat chorus 2 times)

We are invited now

So let us enter in.

No one denied,

None turned away.

The Savior calls to us

So let the feast begin,

Enter the everlasting day.

Ending

Enter the everlasting day.
